# Implementation Verification

After any code change (not documentation-only), before reporting completion:

## 1. Install (if dependencies changed)

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## 2. Run the test suite

```bash
python -m pytest
```

Report pass/fail honestly. Do not claim success without running tests.

## 3. Run configured static / import checks

Run every check defined in `pyproject.toml` (or other project config). At minimum:

```bash
python -c "import app; import app.domain; import app.application; import app.infrastructure; import app.api.main; import app.seed.load"
```

If `[tool.mypy]`, `[tool.ruff]`, `[tool.pyright]`, or similar sections exist in `pyproject.toml`, run those tools and fix or report failures.

## 4. Report

- Test count and outcome
- Any static-check outcome (or state explicitly if none are configured)
- Failures with the relevant output — do not hide errors

## Before every `git push`

**[REQ]** Submission requires raw `.jsonl` session logs in `ai-artifacts/`. Refresh them on every push so the remote always matches the work being pushed.

### Sync Cursor agent transcripts

Copy all session `.jsonl` files from the project’s Cursor transcript folder into `ai-artifacts/` (flat layout; keep original filenames):

```powershell
$src = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE ".cursor\projects\c-Users-Himadri-OneDrive-Desktop-Usual-desktop-stuff-sam-realfast-claims-processing-system\agent-transcripts"
Get-ChildItem $src -Recurse -Filter *.jsonl | Copy-Item -Destination ai-artifacts\ -Force
```

On Unix-like shells, locate the same folder under `~/.cursor/projects/.../agent-transcripts/` and copy `**/*.jsonl` into `ai-artifacts/`.

### Commit with the code

- Include updated `ai-artifacts/*.jsonl` in the commit that precedes the push (same commit as the code, or a dedicated commit immediately before push).
- If a **new** session file appears, add a row to `ai-artifacts/README.md` describing what that session covers.
- Do not push code without syncing logs first unless the human explicitly skips it.

## When to skip

- Documentation-only edits with no code changes (tests still optional; log sync still required before push)
- The human explicitly asked for analysis or planning only
- The human explicitly says to skip log sync for this push
